CHANGES: I rewrote `/agent/solver.md`. The old prompt let the agent stop after about 3 of its 16 model calls, and it often submitted code that failed the public examples or ran too slowly. The new prompt tells it to:
- plan the algorithm and check its complexity before coding;
- always run the public examples first;
- debug by comparing against a brute force on small random inputs;
- time the solution on a max-size input and check edge cases before submitting.

I did not run any trials, so the effect is untested. `validate()` passes.

PREDICTED_DELTA: +4
